  {
   "id": "K-07",
   "src": "easa-cert.jpg (text in image)",
   "kind": "document-text",
   "original": "European Aviation Safety Agency / APPROVAL CERTIFICATE / REFERENCE EASA.145.5139 / Taking into account the provisions of Article 9(2) of Regulation (EC) No 1592/2002 of the European Parliament and of the Council and the bilateral agreements currently in force between European Union Member States and the Government of the United States of America, the European Aviation Safety Agency (EASA) hereby certifies: CONFIDENCE AVIATION INC. FAA Repair Station Number: V9DR072Y 7605 N.W. 50th Street Miami, Florida 33166 USA as a Part-145 maintenance organization approved to maintain the products listed in the FAA Air Agency Certificate and associated Operations Specifications and to issue related certificates of release to service using the above reference, subject to the following conditions: 1. The scope of the approval is limited to that specified on the FAR Part 145 repair station Air Agency Certificate, and the associated Operations Specifications for work carried out in the USA (Unless otherwise agreed in a particular case by EASA). 2. This approval requires continued compliance with FAR Part 145 and the differences as specified in the Maintenance Implementation Procedures, including the use of the FAA Form 8130-3 for release/return to service of components up to and including powerplants. 3. Certificates of return to service must quote the EASA Part 145 approval reference number quoted above and the FAR Part 145 Air Agency Certificate number. 4. Subject to compliance with the foregoing conditions, this approval shall remain valid for an unlimited duration until the approval is surrendered, superseded, suspended or revoked. Date of issue: 19th October 2004. Signed For EASA. EASA Form 3. Page 1 of 1.",
   "en": {
    "pages": [
     "certificates.htm"
    ],
    "text": [
